OL,3,GNEWSACould Somerset pub be the oldest
OL,4,Ain England?
OL,5,
OL,6,FBeing England's oldest pub is a title
OL,7,Fclaimed by a number of establishments
OL,8,Facross the country.
OL,10,FPubs in Nottingham, St Albans and
OL,11,FLincolnshire have all, in the past,
OL,12,Fclaimed to be that very establishment -
OL,13,Fbut one pub in Somerset may have a
OL,14,Fstronger claim than its rivals.
OL,16,FThe George Inn, in Norton St Philip,
OL,17,Fsouth of Bath, is the focus of that
OL,18,Felusive claim of being the country's
OL,19,Foldest pub - thanks to some
OL,20,Finvestigative work by Historic England.
OL,23,APub: 24-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBW-SW Eng NewsC Reg TVFWeather
